			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3878330">
									

<p>A. No. I never implied it. I said it was contributing to the <em>staff's</em> circlejerk. That doesn't explicitly mean that only staff can contribute to it.</p>
<p>B. I can see that. But Clef still seems very much in support of the &quot;movement&quot; per se, and his reasoning just seems like the edgy person who's really a deeply seeded progressive at heart. I was inclined to believe what I was thinking a lot more based on this discussion page, otherwise, I would've given it the benefit of the doubt.</p>
<p>C. I think I've read most of those over the years, but I'll have to refresh my memory of which is which. Just so that we're clear: political elements =/= politically motivated. This is what I'm referring to when I say &quot;apolitical&quot;.</p>

							</div>

								
					
