			<div class="content" id="post-content-3834644">
									

<p>I'm really not sure why people care so much about the &quot;loss&quot; of a frog meme so much.</p>
<p>Frankly, it doesn't matter how much you try and &quot;reclaim it&quot; on the internet. In popular media, it's a lasting symbol of the alt-right, and basically always will be. Unless you're a <strong>hardcore</strong> internet dweller, you probably didn't hear of pepe until it became an Alt-right meme, and you most likely won't ever change it.</p>
<p>Especially since the alt-right is still using it as a symbol, which actively works against your argument.</p>
<p>(Also, I have no idea what that picture is supposed to be of, and the moment I see the word &quot;leftist&quot; I get pretty suspicious of the source.)</p>
<p>Replying to prototype as it's a response to this, and the parent comment.</p>

